{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "id": "09-duplicate-definitions-package-symbol",
  "title": "Duplicate definitions, package-symbol variant: scip-go defines the package symbol api/ in every file of the package",
  "rule_pack": "rules-static-v1",
  "provenance": {
    "kind": "synthetic",
    "source": "hand-authored adversarial static case",
    "seeded_fault": null
  },
  "context": {
    "index": "c034889fbc508e83a67c80d4de6b2cd6693f870eea0972ac369163eb44748423"
  },
  "review_notes": [
    "GetJob is defined once, at api/jobs.go:10. The only symbol with two definition sites is the package symbol `api/` (descriptor ends in `/`, category other), which scip-go emits as a definition in api/jobs.go:1 and api/jobs_legacy.go:1 because that is how Go packages are indexed, not an ambiguity.",
    "scip_duplicate_definition is empty: both duplicate rules join scip_symbol and require category != other, so package (namespace) and `local N` symbols never count as duplicates. claim-duplicate is unresolved with the missing premise scip_symbol (no entity-category row for `api/`).",
    "The exporter's own duplicate check uses the same predicate (_symbol_category != other), so scip_references_closed is emitted for every document and static_reachability_closed is present: the negative authorization-gap claim resolves (supported; the fixture has no authz symbol) instead of being withheld for a wrong reason."
  ],
